.policy "ruff-ruf008-mutable-dataclass-default" revision 2
.description "Give dataclass and attrs fields a default factory instead of a mutable default such as a list, dict or set; one object would be shared by every instance."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff RUF008: a dataclass or attrs field whose default is a mutable value: one object shared by every
// instance (dataclasses even reject a list, dict or set default at runtime). Only annotated fields count; a
// ClassVar is meant to be shared, and an immutable annotation (`Sequence[int]`) says it is not mutated.
//   @dataclass
//   class A:
//       items: list[int] = []                  ← RUF008
//       shared: ClassVar[list[int]] = []       not reported
//       view: Sequence[int] = []               not reported: an immutable annotation
//       untyped = []                           not reported: not a field (RUF012 covers it)
#include "python/ruff-classes.rr"

.violation RUF008(at: node, msg: symbol) code "RUF008" "{msg}"
    suppress ruff "RUF008"
RUF008(v, m) :- dataclass_of(c, k, _), class_field(c, a, _, v), mutable_value(v), field(a, "type", t),
    !class_var_ann(t), !immutable_ann(t), says(k, m).
.decl says(k: symbol, m: symbol)
says("stdlib", "Use `field(default_factory=...)` for this mutable default, or annotate it `ClassVar` if one shared object is intended; a dataclass rejects or shares a plain mutable default.").
says("attrs", "Use `attrs.field(factory=...)` for this mutable default, or annotate it `ClassVar` if one shared object is intended; a plain default is shared by every instance.").
